{"title":"Career roadmap — Cartographer","role":"Cartographer","summary":"A Cartographer specializes in creating, analyzing, and communicating geographic information through maps and spatial visualizations. Modern cartography combines geography, GIS, remote sensing, surveying, spatial databases, satellite imagery, data visualization, and increasingly AI-assisted geospatial analysis.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Geography"},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"★★★★★ — B.Sc. Geography is a strong foundation, but modern Cartographers should add GIS, remote sensing, spatial data, programming, and visualization skills."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build geography, cartography, GIS, surveying and spatial-data fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Cartographer → GIS Analyst → Geospatial Analyst"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Cartographer → GIS Specialist → Geospatial Project Lead"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead digital mapping, 3D geospatial systems, remote sensing and AI-driven mapping"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Physical/human geography, map fundamentals, statistics"},{"text":"Manual mapping, topographic-map interpretation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Cartography, GIS, surveying, remote sensing"},{"text":"QGIS/ArcGIS projects and spatial-data collection"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Spatial databases, GPS, satellite imagery, thematic mapping"},{"text":"GIS/geospatial internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Web GIS, Python, 3D mapping, geospatial analytics"},{"text":"Professional cartography project + portfolio"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Build geographic foundations"},{